Decision recorded: Treat degraded runtime as a blocker to parent Build 1 closure, not as a caveat inside a closed parent issue. Reopened [BUI-1] as `blocked` on [BUI-18] so closure is only valid after live non-degraded verification or explicit unresolved repair blockers. Also recorded that Paperclip API writes must not persist before activity-log failure handling; this needs a transaction or pre-validation of run headers.

## 2026-06-16 15:55:30 — Veyra, CommsOps - Tier 1 lead
Decision recorded: Treat Build 1 as complete only after control-plane behavior, not just issue status, was verified. The previous completion signal was insufficient because Paperclip could mark Codex JSON stream failures as succeeded and could launch Codex without usable `PAPERCLIP_*` shell context. Chose a source-level codex-local adapter fix plus systemd-managed Paperclip handoff instead of relying on per-run manual environment workarounds.

## 2026-06-16 15:32:41 — Veyra, CommsOps - Tier 1 lead
Decision recorded: Treat the prior Build 1 Paperclip state as not complete because successful heartbeat records were masking Codex stream failures. Root causes were the stale `/usr/bin/codex` command path, quota-blocked `gpt-5.3-codex-spark` recovery profile, and stale recovery actions created before owner reassignment. Chose per-agent adapter command overrides and per-agent `cheap` model-profile overrides instead of a broad system PATH mutation.
